{
 "notes": [
  "What the crew say to each other, and where. One exchange is what you get for",
  "pressing somebody's portrait in the crew menu: a line from them, and usually",
  "somebody answering. It is flavour — nothing here changes the state of a game —",
  "which is exactly why it wants a table of its own rather than a branch in the",
  "code.",
  "",
  "An exchange record:",
  "  id     required. Unique. Convention is <where>-<who>[-<n>].",
  "  at     required. Where it can be said:",
  "           a port id  only while docked there",
  "           \"*\"        anywhere, including out in the black",
  "         A port line always beats a \"*\" line, so \"*\" is the thing somebody",
  "         says when they have nothing to say about the view.",
  "  who    required. Whose portrait you pressed: captain, or a berth id",
  "         (engineer, navigator, appraiser). A berth nobody is in has no",
  "         portrait to press, so its lines simply never come up.",
  "  needs  optional. Berth ids who must be aboard for the exchange to be",
  "         reachable — for a line that answers back. `who` is implied.",
  "  lines  required, at least one. [{ who, say }] in order. `who` is any",
  "         speaker, so the captain can answer the navigator and the appraiser",
  "         can talk over both of them.",
  "",
  "Several exchanges can share an `at` and a `who`. Pressing the portrait again",
  "gives the next one, in the order they are written here, and then comes back",
  "round to the first.",
  "",
  "A worked example of what belongs here, in the shape it belongs in:",
  "",
  "  { \"id\": \"cinder-navigator-pistols\", \"at\": \"cinder\", \"who\": \"navigator\",",
  "    \"lines\": [",
  "      { \"who\": \"navigator\", \"say\": \"The plasma pistols here are so shiny.\" },",
  "      { \"who\": \"captain\", \"say\": \"They are. We are not staying long.\" } ] }",
  "",
  "Every line below is a placeholder. The table is the full grid of somewhere by",
  "somebody so that every slot a writer might want already exists; replacing one",
  "is replacing a string, and needs no code and no build beyond the usual one."
 ],
